# four-game football rule (F-college-keys-0007, F-college-keys-0008); NCAA LSDBi bylaw and FBS Oversight Committee reports
src('ncaa_lsdbi_126316', 'NCAA Legislative Services Database (LSDBi), Division I Bylaw 12.8.3.1.6 (renumbered 12.6.3.1.6 on 2025-07-01), https://web3.ncaa.org/lsdbi/bylaw?ruleId=100889&refDate=20260701', 'ncaa-official', True)
src('ncaa_fbsoc_aug24', 'NCAA Division I FBS Oversight Committee, report of the August 22, 2024 videoconference (https://ncaaorg.s3.amazonaws.com/committees/d1/fbsfboc/Aug2024D1FBSOC_Report.pdf)', 'ncaa-official', True)
src('cbs_post24', 'CBS Sports, NCAA rules postseason contests no longer count against four-game max for redshirt eligibility (2024, https://www.cbssports.com/college-football/news/ncaa-rules-postseason-contests-no-longer-count-against-four-game-max-for-redshirt-eligibility/)', 'cbs-sports')
add('F-college-keys-0007', 'ncaa_lsdbi_126316', 'Bylaw text as of refDate 2026-07-01', '12.6.3.1.6 Exception -- Football. [FBS/FCS] In football, a student-athlete representing a Division I institution may compete in up to four contests in a season without using a season of competition.', 4)
add('F-college-keys-0008', 'ncaa_fbsoc_aug24', 'Informational item 1', 'The committee recommended NCAA staff approve a blanket waiver to permit institutions to exempt postseason participation [conference championship game, bowl game, College Football Playoff contest(s)] from the limit of four contests a student-athlete may participate in without using a season of competition for the 2024-25 academic year.')
add('F-college-keys-0008', 'cbs_post24', 'Article body, first paragraph', 'The new rule, which goes into effect immediately for the 2024 seson still limits redshirting players to four games but will not count conference championship, bowl and College Football Playoff contests toward that number.')
note('F-college-keys-0008', 'Read 2026-11-26: the exemption is a blanket waiver renewed year by year (2022-23, 2023-24 and 2024-25 confirmed in the FBS Oversight Committee reports, text saved in research/college/ncaa-primary); the bylaw text itself (LSDBi) states only the four-contest limit. No page read confirms the waiver for 2025-26 or 2026-27.')
note('F-college-keys-0007', 'Read 2026-11-26: the Division I Cabinet adopted the age-based model (Proposal 2026-44, report of 2026-06-23, effective 2026-08-01), which eliminates seasons of competition and redshirt exceptions for students first enrolling full time in 2027-28 and later; students enrolled before or during 2026-27 may still be under the seasons rules, so this row applies to the legacy seasons model only.')

# football fall rule (F-college-keys-0015)
src('ncaa_lsdbi_er2013_7', 'NCAA Legislative Services Database (LSDBi), Division I Proposal ER-2013-7, text of Bylaw 14.4.3.1.6 (adopted 2013-05-28, https://web3.ncaa.org/lsdbi/search/proposalView?id=3069)', 'ncaa-official', True)
add('F-college-keys-0015', 'ncaa_lsdbi_er2013_7', 'Bylaw 14.4.3.1.6 as amended', 'a student-athlete who is a member of the institution\'s football team and who does not successfully complete at least nine-semester hours or eight-quarter hours of academic credit during the fall term and or does not earn the Academic Progress Rate eligibility point for the fall term (or does not successfully complete either requirement) shall not be eligible to compete in the first four contests against outside competition in the following playing season.', 4)
note('F-college-keys-0015', 'Read 2026-11-26: the bylaw text is the 2013 amendment in LSDBi (a current LSDBi page for 14.4.3.1.6 was not found); the NCAA Division I certification criteria PDF (current) still lists the 9 semester / 8 quarter credit-hour fall requirement for football. The 2013 text also allows a one-time regain of eligibility after 27 semester hours before the next fall term (14.4.3.1.6.2). Whether this survives the 2026 age-based model is not stated in the Cabinet reports read.')

# junior college seasons and the age-based clock (F-college-keys-0009)
src('ncaa_agebased', 'NCAA.org, Division I and Division II age-based eligibility rules (https://www.ncaa.org/eligibility-center/division-i-and-division-ii-age-based-eligibility-rules/)', 'ncaa-official', True)
add('F-college-keys-0009', 'ncaa_agebased', 'How the Five-Year Eligibility Period Works', 'Initial full-time college enrollment: The academic term when the student-athlete first enrolls full time and attends class at any college or university, including a domestic institution, international institution or two-year college. ... Once the five-year period starts, it runs continuously. It does not pause because a student-athlete does not compete, transfers, sits out, changes teams or takes time away from participation', True)
note('F-college-keys-0009', 'Answer for the age-based model, read 2026-11-26 on NCAA.org: the five-year period starts at first full-time enrollment at any college including a two-year college and runs continuously, so junior college time counts against the clock under both models.')

