# revenue-share cap and scholarships (F-college-keys-0029, F-college-keys-0030)
src('csc_rs', 'College Sports Commission, Revenue Sharing (https://www.collegesportscommission.org/focus-areas/revenue-sharing/)', 'csc-official', True)
src('fowlkes_csc', 'Fowlkes Firm, What Colleges Need to Know About the New Incremental Scholarship Rules Under the House Settlement (https://www.fowlkesfirm.com/blog/csc)', 'fowlkes-firm')
add('F-college-keys-0029', 'fowlkes_csc', 'Section "The Big Picture"', 'the first $2.5 million in incremental scholarship value (measured by published cost of attendance) counts against the institution\'s revenue-sharing/benefits cap. Any incremental scholarship spending above $2.5M does not count against the cap and is not subject to penalties.', 2500000)
add('F-college-keys-0030', 'csc_rs', 'Footnote under the cap table', '*In 2026-27, a fine of $0.20 for every $1 by which an institution exceeds the cap due to spending on new scholarships created as a result of the removal of scholarship limits (up to $2.5M) will be levied. NCAA Bylaw 16.13.1.8 will then be modified, subject to appropriate NCAA approvals, and cap overages due to an increase in scholarships will not count against the institution\'s cap during the 2027-28 school year and beyond.', 2500000)
note('F-college-keys-0030', 'CONFLICT entered 2026-11-26: the CSC page (primary) and the Fowlkes Firm note say new-scholarship spending up to $2.5M still counts toward the cap in 2026-27 (with a reduced fine of $0.20 per $1 over the cap) and stops counting from 2027-28, which contradicts the 2026-27 value of 0 here (Columbus Dispatch via AOL). The source value recorded for the CSC quote is 2,500,000 (the amount that is fined). The rule key pay.scholarship_credit_2026_27 should be reviewed by the schema integrator: it likely needs 2,500,000 for 2026-27 and 0 from 2027-28.')

