# NCAA Division I Governance Q&A on the House settlement (primary): scholarships and the cap, multiyear agreements
src('ncaa_qa_sep25', 'NCAA Division I Governance, Q&A: Implementation of the House Settlement, updated September 10, 2025 (https://ncaaorg.s3.amazonaws.com/governance/d1/legislation/2024-25/Sep2025D1Gov_PhaseSixSetQuestionandAnswer.pdf; text copy research/college/ncaa-primary/Sep2025D1Gov_PhaseSix_QandA.txt)', 'ncaa-official', True)
src('ncaa_qa_jun25', 'NCAA Division I Governance, Q&A: Implementation of the House Settlement, published June 13, 2025 (https://ncaaorg.s3.amazonaws.com/governance/d1/legislation/2024-25/June2025D1Gov_PhaseThreeInstSetQuestionandAnswer.pdf; text copy research/college/ncaa-primary/June2025D1Gov_PhaseThree_QandA.txt)', 'ncaa-official', True)
add('F-college-keys-0029', 'ncaa_qa_sep25', 'Question D9', 'Yes, up to $2.5 million of new incremental athletically related financial aid (e.g., scholarships) above the Division I institutional financial aid limits in the 2024-25 Division I Manual will count against the benefits cap each year. Beyond $2.5 million, new incremental athletically related financial aid beyond the Division I institutional financial aid limits in the 2024-25 Division I Manual will not count against the cap.', 2500000)
add('F-college-keys-0031', 'ncaa_qa_jun25', 'Question D20', 'Additional payments promised in multiyear agreements are counted against a Participating Institution\'s benefits cap in the year that the payments and/or benefits are provided.', True)
add('F-college-keys-0031', 'ncaa_qa_sep25', 'Question D26', 'Is there a maximum term for an NIL contract or payment between a Participating Institution and a current or prospective student-athlete? Yes. The term of the agreement may not be longer than the prospective or current student-athlete\'s period of eligibility to participate in intercollegiate athletics.', True)
note('F-college-keys-0031', 'Primary text read 2026-11-26 (NCAA Division I Governance Q&A, June and September 2025): multiyear agreements are allowed and count against the cap in the year paid; the maximum term is the student-athlete\'s remaining period of eligibility (D26, NIL agreements).')
note('F-college-keys-0030', 'The NCAA Division I Governance Q&A of 2025-09-10 (D9) says the $2.5 million of new aid counts against the benefits cap "each year", with no 2026-27 carve-out.')

